  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The third side is parallel to a bisector of the angle between equal sides.</p><p>The bisectors are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>7</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><msqrt><msup><mn>7</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>&#177;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><msqrt><msup><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>7</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>&#177;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>7</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>&#177;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>18</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Let the third side be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></math> or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>L</mi></math></p><p>It passes through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>)</mo></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>31</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn></math></p><p>Hence, required lines are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>31</mn></math>&nbsp;or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn></math>.&nbsp;</p>",
